/T (Looking ahead, the latter half of 2025 is likely to witness tactical evolution over sheer volume. With cybersecurity teams hardening defenses, ransomware groups may pivot toward supply chain vulnerabilities and software exploits \(as seen in several CVE disclosures across forums\), aiming for maximum lateral spread with minimal exposure. Organizations, especially those in critical infrastructure and financial services, must prioritize proactive threat intelligence and simulated response drills to mitigate the risks ahead.)
/E (Looking ahead, the latter half of 2025 is likely to witness tactical evolution over sheer volume. With cybersecurity teams hardening defenses, ransomware groups may pivot toward supply chain vulnerabilities and software exploits \(as seen in several CVE disclosures across forums\), aiming for maximum lateral spread with minimal exposure. Organizations, especially those in critical infrastructure and financial services, must prioritize proactive threat intelligence and simulated response drills to mitigate the risks ahead.)
