/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (Security researchers uncovered four high-severity flaws in Gigabyte motherboard firmware that expose the system to persistent firmware-level attacks. Exploited via System Management Mode \(SMM\), these bugs allow attackers to bypass Secure Boot and install stealth malware that survives reboots or reinstalls. Affected systems include numerous consumer and enterprise devices. Given the difficulty in detecting and removing such implants, BIOS updates have been issued and are strongly recommended.)
/E (Security researchers uncovered four high-severity flaws in Gigabyte motherboard firmware that expose the system to persistent firmware-level attacks. Exploited via System Management Mode \(SMM\), these bugs allow attackers to bypass Secure Boot and install stealth malware that survives reboots or reinstalls. Affected systems include numerous consumer and enterprise devices. Given the difficulty in detecting and removing such implants, BIOS updates have been issued and are strongly recommended.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
